If equals returns true, the two objects must have the same hashCode. Unequal objects may still collide; a hash code is not a unique identifier. Records generate compatible equals and hashCode implementations.

hashCode() takes no arguments and returns an int hash. After the Key record declaration shown below, this checks the equal-value requirement without assuming any particular hash number:
```java
Key first = new Key(3);
Key second = new Key(3);
System.out.println(first.hashCode() == second.hashCode());
```
Output: true.

